#    land writes: - OUTCOME-CHECK DUE <key> <sha> — task:<slug> by:<YYYY-MM-DD> expect:>=<N>|infer — outcome: <o> — check: <cmd>
#    On or after its by-day (Central): the read-only gate passes the check or it is never run (COULDNT-CHECK); CODE runs
#    it (file-write sandbox, 5 min), counts its output, and alone decides COULDNT-CHECK (the command failed or printed
#    nothing; exit 1 with one bare integer is a count) and FAIL (count below the floor); a PASS is then
#    impossible. Only a count at or over the floor goes to ONE fresh `ai-run --role brain`, which judges whether that
#    output really is the outcome and posts `Outcome check (live): PASS|FAIL|COULDNT-CHECK — <what it saw, with counts>`.
